1.3.2 Discovering latent “factors of variation”
When dealing with high-dimensional data, it is often useful to reduce the dimensionality by projecting it to a lower dimensional subspace which captures the “essence” of the data. One approach to this problem is to assume that each observed high-dimensional output xn ∈ RD was generated by a set
